# Q4 Release Complete

We've just rolled out [our Q4 release](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=previous-release-notes), while there are a lot of new features you may want to take advantage of. Here I want to focus on the developer relevant features and improvements:

* New v3.2.x client libraries for Python, C# is next. Updated Java and node.js client libraries. Almost all of the v1 API is now supported by all our client libraries. See the [updated Zuora client libraries](/docs/guides/libraries/), and our [Get Started](/docs/get-started/introduction/) and use case driven [Tutorials](/docs/get-started/tutorials/). We're investing in adding more tutorials and creating 'Skill Paths', watch that space.
* [Easier notification management](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=platform-events-and-notifications-overview), including the ability to create custom filters on the out of the box notifications. Also changes to notifications are now tracked by audit trail and reportable.
* [Auto generate credit card surcharge fees](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=payments-payment-schedules) (where legal) in EA.
* [Simpler, low or no code, payment capture forms](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=payments-payment-form-overview) in EA, though not all gateways are supported yet.
* Share [invoice specific payment links](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=payments-overview-of-zuora-payment-link) with your customers
* [Deployment Manager now integrates with git, GitHub](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=platform-source-code-integration-with-deployment-manager) specifically to start, other repositories to follow.
* New [Workday Financials connector](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=platform-zuora-connector-for-workday-financials).
* New Apple App Store, Google Play Store and Roku Pay connectors in EA, bring all those transactions into Zuora for a unified subscription view regardless of channel. Talk to your Zuora team for more information.
* [14 data warehousing connectors](https://docs.zuora.com?resourceId=platform-available-connectors), run, don't walk, run from having to support you home grown connector. You're too valuable.
* We've simplified our [concurrency limits](/docs/guides/rate-limits/#concurrent-request-limits).
* Much more detail in the [v1 API Release Notes](/docs/get-started/changelogs/v1-api-changelog/)

You do know we've moved away from twice-monthly releases to a quarterly release cadence, right?



**Richard Sawey**
Developer Advocate
